  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers pay for people who learn fast and work well in teams. They judge you by consistent behaviour across tests, discussions and interviews.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is telling one true story about a result you produced with others.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and management trainee and leadership programmes: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools help with practice questions and mock interviews. Generic answers will sound alike.
  </p>
  <p>
    Honest stories, teamwork and judgment hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to practise; later, own your stories and decisions.
  </p>

